{"type":"text","timestamp":1788516608860,"sessionID":"ses_f941b7113ffesExH89VltYe1dh","part":{"id":"prt_06be59459001eXqMZbzUJ3hCDz","messageID":"msg_06be57313001jTfplaX76JQdAb","sessionID":"ses_f941b7113ffesExH89VltYe1dh","type":"text","text":"Reviewed all five scripts and verified behavior by execution.\n\n**Verified defects:**\n- `api.sh:1` — no JSON escaping. `public_response 'a\",\"admin\":true'` emits `{\"name\":\"a\",\"admin\":true\"}`, letting caller-controlled input inject arbitrary JSON fields; `\"` and `\\` also produce invalid JSON.\n- `pagination.sh:1` — the regex accepts leading zeros but `(( ))` then evaluates the value as octal: `08` errors out (\"value too great for base\") and is rejected, while `010` and `0100` validate as 8 and 64 rather than 10 and 100.\n\n**Verified correct (no findings):**\n- `authorization.sh` — owner check is enforced before any value is emitted; returns 3 on mismatch, 0 with value on match.\n- `counter.sh` — `flock` creates the lock file and holds it for the whole read-modify-write; 50 concurrent increments yielded exactly 50.\n- `storage.sh` — the backend's exit status propagates unchanged (`false` → rc 1), which is the documented \"or fail\" contract.\n\n{\"findings\":[{\"file\":\"api.sh\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"summary\":\"public_response interpolates its argument into JSON without escaping, so input containing a double quote can inject arbitrary JSON fields or emit invalid JSON.\"},{\"file\":\"pagination.sh\",\"severity\":\"material\",\"summary\":\"validate_page_size accepts leading zeros in the regex but evaluates them as octal in the arithmetic test, so '08' errors and is rejected while '010' and '0100' are validated as 8 and 64.\"}]}","time":{"start":1788516602969,"end":1788516608855}}}
